{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.32.7.a001", "note": "Explicit subject takes only its pronoun; the copula goes to the predicate (rule 20).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.7.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.7.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.32.7.a002", "note": "Predicate noun takes the copula (rule 20); 'hiding place' heads on 'hiding' since 'place' alone is any place (rule 31).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.7.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.7.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.32.7.a003", "note": "Possessive dative recast as the possessive 'my'; the preposition is left with nothing (rule 40).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.7.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.7.003", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.32.7.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.7.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.7.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.32.7.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.7.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.7.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006", "t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.32.7.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.7.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.7.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.32.7.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.7.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.7.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.32.7.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.7.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.7.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.32.7.a009", "note": "'compass ... about' read as the ASV's phrasal rendering of סָבַב; 'about' restates the surrounding the verb writes and stays with it (rule 44), discontinuous around the object. Competing reading marks 'about' added.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.7.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.7