{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.32.8.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a004", "note": "Subject and auxiliary written once for the coordinated verbs; this verb takes only its lexical word.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a007", "note": "Supplied 'the' belongs to the noun (rule 15); no article morpheme present.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a008", "note": "Relative זוּ takes 'which'.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a010", "note": "Cohortative verb with its subject and auxiliary (rule 17).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015", "t016", "t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a011", "note": "Supplied object 'thee' of 'counsel'; no object morpheme on the verb (the suffix on עַל is realized by the later 'thee'), so it is added under rule 44.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a012", "note": "Bare circumstantial nominal takes the supplied 'with' (rule 33), discontinuous around the possessive.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.013"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019", "t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.014"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a014", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "PSA.32.8.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.8.012"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.8.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}], "ref": "PSA.32.8", "review_notes": ["The ASV reads 'I will counsel thee with mine eye upon thee'; the first 'thee' is a supplied object, the second realizes the suffix on עָלֶיךָ."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.32.9.a001", "note": "Imperative-jussive with its subject pronoun 'ye' written after the verb (rules 17, 36).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a004", "note": "Supplied 'the' belongs to the noun (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a005", "note": "No conjunction stands between the two comparative phrases; the 'or' is a supplied coordinator (rule 14).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a008", "note": "Relative supplied over an asyndetic clause with a written antecedent; no relative, suffix or pronoun in the clause licenses it (rules 46, 55).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a009", "note": "Negative existential recast possessively 'have no'; the existential takes the frame and heads on the negation (rules 43, 50).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a011", "note": "The ASV's identity recasting leaves the instrumental בְּ without an English relation. Must be is a construction-supplied modal copula, not an independent rendering of with.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.009", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a012", "note": "The opening nominal predicate takes must be bit under rule 20. The competing reading assigns the frame to בְּ, although the ASV leaves its instrumental relation unstated.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017", "t018", "t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a013", "note": "Retained conjunction and.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a014", "note": "Retained coordinated predicate bridle.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.012"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a015", "note": "Retained subject nominal trappings.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.013"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a016", "note": "Retained suffix recast as Whose under rule 18.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.014"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.015"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a018", "note": "'hold ... in' is the phrasal rendering of בָּלַם (restrain); 'in' completes what bare 'hold' does not write (rule 44).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.016"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023", "t025"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a019", "note": "Supplied object of the infinitive; no object morpheme is written (rule 44).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a020", "note": "Italic 'Else' is a supplied connective for an asyndetic clause (rule 14); margin 'That they come not near' set aside (rule 38).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t026"], "target_head": "t026"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a021", "note": "Infinitive recast as a finite clause takes the supplied subject and modal (rules 48, 52); 'come near' heads on the complement carrying the lexeme of קָרַב (rule 44). Competing head: 'come'.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.018"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t027", "t028", "t030", "t031"], "target_head": "t031"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a022", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.017"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t029"], "target_head": "t029"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a023", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.019"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t032"], "target_head": "t032"}, {"id": "PSA.32.9.a024", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.32.9.020"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.32.9.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t033"], "target_head": "t033"}], "ref": "PSA.32.9", "review_notes": ["The ASV heavily recasts the second colon; the copula placement on בְּ is the least settled unit and the alternative is named in its note."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
